{"c":{"36309":["Narrator",null,"b36309-6KM0riV4lqfN.jpg","This character page is set to represent and list all narrators, which haven't been given a visual representation of themselves in their respective work.",2200],"279994":["Piast","Male","b279994-0R7MExJ68wv8.png","",14],"279995":["Kolbe","Male","b279995-4n4fhISlYg9Z.png","",1],"279996":["Nowak","Male","b279996-MdHZp8RFDafh.png","Novak is a former mercenary and current inquisitor. He doesn't particularly believe in the church's dogma, but wants to maintain a peaceful society for the sake of his daughter.",804],"279997":["Potocki","Male","b279997-Ja3sncvWGwvC.png","Rafal's adoptive father. He knew that Rafal was researching the heliocentric theory and tolerated it.",11],"279998":["Jolenta","Female","b279998-Jxzcihblmclf.png","Jolenta is an astronomy research assistant. She is restricted in her studies because she is a woman.",403],"279999":["Badeni","Male","b279999-VKadGXZplQiE.png","Badeni is a monk in search of the \"moment that makes life special.\" As a result of that, his eyes were burned out and he was moved to a rural village. He has an extraordinary amount of knowledge and the ability to calculate.",937],"280000":["Hubert","Male","b280000-aLUMhQNkdr0J.png","Hubert is a scholar who was arrested as a heretic for his research on the geocentric theory. He was taken in by Potocki on the pretense that he had reformed, but continued his astronomical observations with Rafal, whom he met when he was released.",33],"280001":["Rafał","Male","b280001-40iXrV4vLyqR.png","Rafal is a child prodigy who at the age of twelve was planning to advance to college and major in theology. One day, he meets Hubert and is fascinated by the beauty of the heliocentric theory.",975],"280002":["Oczy","Male","b280002-3E9GkKZ8YH9D.png","Pessimistic and afraid of looking up at the sky, this private police duelist by trade goes on an unlikely astronomical quest. “Oczy” is the plural word of “oko”, the Polish word for “eye”.",680],"280003":